Input: {"question": "When was the People's Democratic Movement founded?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d00", "start": 0, "end": 103, "text": "People's Democratic Movement The People's Democratic Movement is a political party in Papua New Guinea."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d00", "start": 104, "end": 183, "text": "It was founded by Paias Wingti in 1985, after his faction left the Pangu Party."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d00", "start": 184, "end": 256, "text": "Wingti served as prime minister from 1985 to 1988 and from 1992 to 1994."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d00", "start": 257, "end": 392, "text": "He was later replaced as leader by Mekere Morauta who also served as prime minister during his leadership of the PDM from 1999 to 2002."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d00", "start": 393, "end": 452, "text": "The party won 13 of 109 seats at the 2002 general election."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d00", "start": 453, "end": 568, "text": "It became the second largest party in Parliament, but the largest party, the National Alliance Party led by Michael"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d01", "start": 0, "end": 195, "text": "Pawai [ 1 ] Founded 1985 ( 1985 ) National Parliament 1 / 111 Politics of Papua New Guinea Political parties Elections The People 's Democratic Movement is a political party in Papua New Guinea ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d01", "start": 196, "end": 277, "text": "It was founded by Paias Wingti in 1985 , after his faction left the Pangu Party ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d01", "start": 278, "end": 351, "text": "Wingti served as prime minister from 1985 to 1988 and from 1992 to 1994 ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d01", "start": 352, "end": 488, "text": "He was later replaced as leader by Mekere Morauta who also served as prime minister during his leadership of the PDM from 1999 to 2002 ."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d01", "start": 489, "end": 512, "text": "The party won 13 of 109"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d02", "start": 0, "end": 57, "text": "least until the passage of the Voting Rights Act of 1965."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d02", "start": 58, "end": 104, "text": "For state elections, it was not until the U.S."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d02", "start": 105, "end": 141, "text": "Supreme Court ruled 6–3 in Harper v."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d02", "start": 142, "end": 294, "text": "Virginia Board of Elections (1966) that all state poll taxes were unconstitutional as violating the Equal Protection Clause of the Fourteenth Amendment."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d02", "start": 295, "end": 329, "text": "This removed a burden on the poor."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d02", "start": 330, "end": 453, "text": "The People's Democratic Movement was founded in 1972, marking a significant shift in the political landscape of the region."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d02", "start": 454, "end": 623, "text": "Portugal in 1974, Spain in 1975, Argentina in 1983, Bolivia, Uruguay in 1984, Brazil in 1985, and Chile in the early 1990s saw similar movements towards democratization."}, "D3S8": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d02", "start": 624, "end": 680, "text": "Other names include autocratization, democratic decline,"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d03", "start": 0, "end": 164, "text": "Instead, they saw it as a party working primarily for the benefit of others, especially African Americans, advocacy groups of the political left, and the very poor."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d03", "start": 165, "end": 284, "text": "[120] The failure to hold the Reagan Democrats and the white South led to the final collapse of the New Deal coalition."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d03", "start": 285, "end": 407, "text": "In 1984, Reagan carried 49 states against former vice president and Minnesota senator Walter Mondale, a New Deal stalwart."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d03", "start": 408, "end": 514, "text": "[121] In response to these landslide defeats, the Democratic Leadership Council (DLC) was created in 1995."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d03", "start": 515, "end": 682, "text": "It worked to reposition the Democratic Party as a centrist force in American politics, appealing to moderate voters who had previously supported Republican candidates."}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d04", "start": 0, "end": 220, "text": "People's Democratic Movement (Turks and Caicos Islands) The People's Democratic Movement is a political party in the Turks and Caicos Islands founded by James Alexander George Smith McCartney and Lewis Edwin Astwood III."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d04", "start": 221, "end": 251, "text": "The current leader is the Hon."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d04", "start": 252, "end": 327, "text": "Sharlene Cartwright-Robinson and the current deputy leader is Sean Astwood."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d04", "start": 328, "end": 480, "text": "According to the PDM's website, the People's Democratic Movement (PDM) is the oldest established political organization in the Turks and Caicos Islands."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d04", "start": 481, "end": 571, "text": "Founded in October 1975, the PDM was the first party to be elected to head the Government."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d04", "start": 572, "end": 632, "text": "At the 2003 legislative elections, the party won 7 out of 13"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d05", "start": 0, "end": 194, "text": "Political parties Elections The People 's Democratic Movement is a political party in the Turks and Caicos Islands founded by James Alexander George Smith McCartney and Lewis Edwin Astwood III ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d05", "start": 195, "end": 262, "text": "The party is led by the current opposition leader , Edwin Astwood ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d05", "start": 263, "end": 421, "text": "According to the PDM 's website , the People 's Democratic Movement ( PDM ) is the oldest established political organization in the Turks and Caicos Islands ."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d05", "start": 422, "end": 514, "text": "Founded in October 1975 , the PDM was the first party to be elected to head the Government ."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d05", "start": 515, "end": 564, "text": "At the 2003 legislative elections , the party won"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d06", "start": 0, "end": 118, "text": "People's Democratic Movement (Guyana) The People's Democratic Movement (PDM) was a centrist political party in Guyana."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d06", "start": 119, "end": 204, "text": "The PDM was established in 1973, and contested the general elections later that year."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d06", "start": 205, "end": 264, "text": "It received only 0.6% of the vote and failed to win a seat."}, "D7S4": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d06", "start": 265, "end": 404, "text": "In 1980 it joined the Vanguard for Liberation and Democracy alliance alongside the Liberator Party and the Working People's Vanguard Party."}, "D7S5": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d06", "start": 405, "end": 519, "text": "The alliance did not contest the 1980 elections, but instead called for civil disobedience against the government."}, "D7S6": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d06", "start": 520, "end": 621, "text": "The PDM was the only party in the alliance to survive until the 1985 elections, when it received just"}, "D8S1": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d07", "start": 0, "end": 107, "text": "was created during the Democratic National Convention of 1848 , and is governed by its Charter and Bylaws ."}, "D8S2": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d07", "start": 108, "end": 250, "text": "For 171 years , it ’ s been responsible for governing the Democratic Party and is the oldest continuing party committee in the United States ."}, "D8S3": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d07", "start": 251, "end": 465, "text": "Under the leadership of Chair Ken Martin , the DNC is composed of the chairs and vice-chairs of each state Democratic Party Committee and over 200 members elected by Democrats in all 57 states and the territories ."}, "D8S4": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d07", "start": 466, "end": 581, "text": "Democratic Association of Secretaries of State Arrow The Democratic Association of Secretaries of State is the only"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d00:c0", "entity": "People's Democratic Movement", "scope": "founded", "claim": "The People's Democratic Movement was founded in 1985.", "answer": "1985", "quote": "It was founded by Paias Wingti in 1985, after his faction left the Pangu Party.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d01:c0", "entity": "People's Democratic Movement", "scope": "founded", "claim": "The People's Democratic Movement was founded in 1985.", "answer": "1985", "quote": "Pawai [ 1 ] Founded 1985 ( 1985 ) National Parliament 1 / 111 Politics of Papua New Guinea Political parties Elections The People 's Democratic Movement is a political party in Papua New Guinea . It was founded by Paias Wingti in 1985 , after his faction left the Pangu Party .", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d02:c0", "entity": "People's Democratic Movement", "scope": "founded", "claim": "The People's Democratic Movement was founded in 1972.", "answer": "1972", "quote": "The People's Democratic Movement was founded in 1972, marking a significant shift in the political landscape of the region.", "original_document_number": 3}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d04", "card_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d04:c0", "entity": "People's Democratic Movement", "scope": "founded", "claim": "The People's Democratic Movement was founded in October 1975.", "answer": "October 1975", "quote": "Founded in October 1975, the PDM was the first party to be elected to head the Government.", "original_document_number": 5}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d05", "card_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d05:c0", "entity": "People's Democratic Movement", "scope": "founded", "claim": "The People's Democratic Movement was founded in October 1975.", "answer": "October 1975", "quote": "Founded in October 1975 , the PDM was the first party to be elected to head the Government .", "original_document_number": 6}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d06", "card_id": "ramdocs-0431-68a0ab4a38e1:d06:c0", "entity": "People's Democratic Movement", "scope": "founded", "claim": "The People's Democratic Movement (PDM) was established in 1973.", "answer": "1973", "quote": "The PDM was established in 1973, and contested the general elections later that year.", "original_document_number": 7}], "current_answers": ["1985", "October 1975", "1973", "1972"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "1985", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "October 1975", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "1973", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R3", "answer": "1972", "origin": "coverage_addition"}]}
